The result is **FINDINGS**: startup works on the current build, but some checks weren't done and there is one minor audio warning. The report is at `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.32cQhq/report.md`.

- **Server:** Port 8000 was free, so I started a server on `dist/` myself. `make -n` shows nothing to rebuild, and the `web/` files match `dist/`. The `doom.wasm` hash matches the prior run. I stopped the server afterwards and the port is free again.
- **Loading:** All 6 assets returned 200 within 26 ms. The page title is "DOOM Shareware" and the canvas is 640x400.
- **Startup:** The title screen appeared right after load, with correct colours and no corruption. That closes the open question from the prior review about whether the title frame shows on this build. The frame counter went from 378 to 443 in one second, so the loop is running.
- **Console:** 0 errors and 2 warnings. Both warnings are the AudioContext "not allowed to start before a user gesture" message, which is expected under autoplay policy. The owner is `coder_input_audio`, and I didn't check that audio resumes after a gesture.
- **Not verified:** Precise time to first frame, a clean rebuild, other browsers, warm-cache reload, other viewports and audio after a gesture. Movement and combat are out of scope for this role.

I wrote nothing outside `OUTPUT_DIR` except the Playwright captures in `artifacts/browser/`. Evidence in `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.32cQhq/` includes `early.png`, `console.txt` and `server.log`.